MISSION

Harden the current Files / software-package user experience across the two
existing operating environments:

- NODE-OS Files
- RACK-OS Files

The underlying filesystem, download, and software-installation mechanics already
exist.

This slice improves how those real mechanics are presented and operated.

Primary problems to solve:

- software package details currently feel visually raw
- INSTALL / INSTALLED states need a clear technical action grammar
- DOWNLOAD / DOWNLOADED states need the same quality
- long paths and release IDs must remain readable on mobile
- action controls should look native to their operating environment rather than
  generic browser buttons
- metadata hierarchy should be easier to scan
- NODE-OS and RACK-OS should express the same underlying truth without becoming
  identical interfaces

This is a UX / presentation hardening slice.

Do not change the underlying gameplay lifecycle merely to improve presentation.


